  "ingredients": [
    "2/3 cup frozen spinach (thawed and drained)",
    "3 large egg",
    "1/2 cup cheddar cheese (shredded)",
    "1/4 cup fresh cilantro (chopped)",
    "1 cup nutritional yeast",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 350 degrees Farenheit. Make sure that all excess water is squeezed out of the spinach.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spinach-and-cheese-bites/#wprm-recipe-53004-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/spinach-bites-1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine spinach in a mixing bowl with the eggs, cheese, cilantro, nutritional yeast, salt, and pepper. Make sure it’s mixed together well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spinach-and-cheese-bites/#wprm-recipe-53004-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/spinach-bites-2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Scoop out tablespoons of the batter and roll into balls. Place on a greased cookie sheet. The dough is very sticky, but if it gives you too much trouble then feel free to sprinkle in a little almond or coconut flour. You can also wet your hands to help with rolling",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spinach-and-cheese-bites/#wprm-recipe-53004-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/spinach-bites-3.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 20 minutes at 350°F. The bites will be firm and browned on the bottom.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spinach-and-cheese-bites/#wprm-recipe-53004-step-0-3",
